<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="080" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rule set and rate card scope schema: core lookups, scope options, all-BU flag, BU N:N, rate card scope and backfill</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172), wave W3-6</phase>
    <gate>blocked: owner approval of the final script required before running</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New idempotent schema script on dev (additive columns, options, one N:N) plus a data backfill of an existing column-less table; no BFF code. The backfill writes rows, so the run is owner-gated.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Every item, name and value is fixed by the design note section 2; the scripts it copies already exist in scripts/ebilling/.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live dev schema change on two tables other tasks read (sprk_ruleset, sprk_ratecard), gated by an owner approval and coordinated with ontology-r1 and uac-r2.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>019, 017, 029</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, schema, coordination</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Write scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1, which adds items S1-S4 and S6 of notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 2 to dev (core-record lookups on sprk_ruleset with RemoveLink, the Record and FirmRecord scope options, the all-business-units flag, the sprk_ruleset-businessunit N:N, and a new explicit scope on sprk_ratecard with a one-time backfill), and update the two data-model docs. Show the final script and its -WhatIf output to the owner and run it only after the owner approves.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Dataverse metadata Web API, idempotent schema scripts on EbillingSchema.psm1, and coordinating changes with the projects that read the same tables.</role>

  <goal>After owner approval, dev has every S1-S4 and S6 item with the stated names, types, values and delete behaviour; every existing sprk_ratecard row has a scope set by the backfill rule, or is listed as not set; a second run writes nothing; docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md and sprk_ratecard.md describe the new columns and the fail-closed rule; ontology-r1 and uac-r2 had a notice before and after the run.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 2, 3.5 and 4.5. Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171 (levels, BU filter), D-137 / ontology D-172 (direct inheritance; no delete-Restrict; explicit scope on rule sets AND rate cards; GitHub #2129, #2132, DEF-027). sprk_ruleset today: sprk_scope local choice ClientDefault 100000000, Firm 100000001; sprk_firm RemoveLink (docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md:29-30). sprk_ratecard today: optional sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_workassignment lookups, RemoveLink on dev, no scope column (docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md:17-20); RateCardResolver derives the scope from the lookups (RateCardResolver.cs:133-142).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/EbillingSchema.psm1 (Add-Lookup :334, Add-LocalChoice :467, Add-ManyToMany :777; module default delete RemoveLink :337)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingTimekeeperRateCardSchema.ps1:431-436 (the three core lookups to copy)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingApprovalSchema.ps1:168 (N:N precedent)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingSubmissionIntegrityOption.ps1 (insert an option, refuse relabel or renumber)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingPolicyStoreSchema.ps1 (two-option column with a default)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="completed">sprk_ruleset table and sprk_scope choice</dependency>
      <dependency task="017" status="completed">sprk_ratecard table and its core lookups</dependency>
      <dependency task="029" status="completed">WP1 schema in dev and SpaarkeMaster</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 (#2132)">No delete-Restrict anywhere in this script. The three sprk_ruleset core lookups (S1) use RemoveLink, the module default; the three sprk_ratecard core lookups are not touched. Quote in the script header: "Deleting a matter must never require first deleting its rate cards or rule sets, because the user may lack permission."</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S1">sprk_ruleset.sprk_matter → sprk_matter, sprk_project → sprk_project, sprk_workassignment → sprk_workassignment; relationships sprk_matter_ruleset_matter, sprk_project_ruleset_project, sprk_workassignment_ruleset_workassignment; optional.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S2, D-172">Insert sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope options Record = 100000002 and FirmRecord = 100000003. ClientDefault 100000000 and Firm 100000001 are unchanged. If either value or label exists with another meaning, refuse (copy Deploy-EbillingSubmissionIntegrityOption.ps1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S3">sprk_ruleset.sprk_allbusinessunits: two-option, display "All business units", default Yes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S4 (Q2, approved with the script)">N:N sprk_ruleset_businessunit between sprk_ruleset and businessunit. Pre-check EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='businessunit')?$select=CanBeInManyToMany: if false, STOP (escalation), do not create a fallback table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S6, D-172, DEF-027">sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope: new local choice, display "Applies to", Firm = 100000000, CoreRecord = 100000001, optional, no default. Backfill only rows whose sprk_scope is empty: exactly one core lookup → CoreRecord; none → Firm; two or more → leave empty and list. Never overwrite a set value. The output lists every card marked Firm (name, id, firm) for the owner.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md section 5, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Owner approval required before running the script for real: show the final script and the -WhatIf output and wait for an explicit OK. Dev only. -WhatIf first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md section 3 (pipeline)">Do NOT edit src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/** (079 syncs it). No forms or views here (079). No plugins, business rules or calculated columns (ADR-002). S5 (config/secure-record-owner-role.json) is task 081's, not this script's.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md (sections 2, 3.5, 4.5)</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Ebilling schema script" location="scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingTimekeeperRateCardSchema.ps1">Initialize-EbillingSchema, check-then-create per item, -WhatIf, a tally at the end, publish.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Collision check on dev: sprk_ruleset (sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment, sprk_allbusinessunits, sprk_scope option values 100000002-100000003), sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope, relationship and intersect names, businessunit CanBeInManyToMany. Record the results in notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the script on EbillingSchema.psm1, copying the reference scripts named in relevant-files. S1, S2, S3, S4, then S6 column, then the S6 backfill (a separate section with its own -WhatIf output and its list of cards marked Firm, CoreRecord and left empty).</step>
    <step order="3">Notice before: post the planned item list and the -WhatIf output to ontology-r1 and uac-r2 (a comment on #2129 and a message to each session). Record the date.</step>
    <step order="4">Owner approval: show the owner the final script and the -WhatIf output, including the backfill list. Wait for an explicit OK; record it with the date in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="5">Run for real, then run again: the second run reports no created item and writes no row.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify by metadata read: every column, option value, the N:N, and the RemoveLink delete behaviour on the three new sprk_ruleset relationships. Verify by data read: no sprk_ratecard row whose scope was set before the run changed.</step>
    <step order="7">Notice after: send the run result and the backfill list to ontology-r1 and uac-r2.</step>
    <step order="8">Update docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md (S1-S4, the four scope values, "a Record / FirmRecord set whose lookup is cleared applies to nothing") and sprk_ratecard.md (S6, the backfill rule, RemoveLink kept, "an empty scope or a CoreRecord card with no lookup is never used").</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner has not approved the final script, STOP before step 5. Do not run anything except -WhatIf.</trigger>
    <trigger>If businessunit reports CanBeInManyToMany = false, STOP and ask the owner to approve option (b) of the design note (an intersect table) as a script change; do not create it on your own.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any planned name or option value exists with another meaning, STOP and present both to the owner; do not rename or renumber.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the backfill finds a card with two or more core lookups, list it and leave it empty; do not choose one.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope (019) and sprk_ratecard's optional core lookups (017) exist; grep of scripts/ebilling and docs/data-model finds no core lookup on sprk_ruleset, no business-unit link and no rate card scope column.</existing>
    <extension>The existing choice gains two options instead of a new column; the rate card gets the same explicit-scope idea the rule set already has. The BU list needs a relationship, because no existing column can hold a set of business units with referential integrity.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A rule set cannot name a matter, project or work assignment (D-171), and a rate card whose record is deleted keeps applying firm-wide to every invoice of that firm (#2132, DEF-027).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Schema script</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Metadata and row reads</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="script">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md, docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md, projects/ebilling-r1/notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task notes record the owner's explicit approval of the final script, with the date, before the real run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A dev metadata read shows the three sprk_ruleset core lookups with relationships named as in S1 and delete behaviour RemoveLink (not Restrict); sprk_scope has exactly ClientDefault 100000000, Firm 100000001, Record 100000002, FirmRecord 100000003; sprk_allbusinessunits defaults to Yes; the N:N sprk_ruleset_businessunit exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope exists with exactly Firm 100000000 and CoreRecord 100000001 and no default; the three sprk_ratecard core relationships still read RemoveLink.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After the backfill, every card with exactly one core lookup reads CoreRecord, every card with none reads Firm, and any card with two or more is empty and listed in the notes; the notes list every card marked Firm.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A second run creates nothing and writes no row; a row whose scope was set before the run is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/ and no file under src/ changed; config/secure-record-owner-role.json unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notices to ontology-r1 and uac-r2 before and after the run are recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both data-model docs describe the new columns and the fail-closed rule.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Until 085 deploys, RateCardResolver ignores sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope, so the backfill changes no behaviour. 079 re-runs the backfill section (idempotent) immediately before deploying the BFF, to catch cards the old import created in between. Q2 (N:N storage) is approved together with this script; it is not an open design question.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
